23:26:49.736 SET-FIELD PROBE IS ON - which by now means 'the channel answers at all'. The
23:26:49.736   flag is a misnomer kept for the launch line: without it Session::handle
23:26:49.736   returns nothing for every packet, so the migration hello goes unanswered and
23:26:49.736   the client freezes on 'Connecting...'.
23:26:49.736   With it on, this channel answers: the migration hello with a SetField
23:26:49.736   carrying the character's real record (presence[0] the stat block, presence[2]
23:26:49.736   the equipped list), 0x00DC with that field's NPCs and mobs, 0x00D1 with the
23:26:49.736   portal's destination, 0x00E7 with the !map GM command, and 0x0151 with a
23:26:49.736   script Say, 0x0104 with the NPC shop, and 0x00D2 with a channel migration.
23:26:49.736   CONFIRMED on a real client: the dressed character, the bag and its 125 slots,
23:26:49.736   NPC dialogue, mobs spawning and moving, an unequip that survives a map change.
23:26:49.736   NOT yet seen on screen: the shop counter, the quest journal, the channel
23:26:49.736   switch. Dropping an item is refused on purpose - there is nowhere to put it.
